1
00:00:07,77 --> 00:00:10,33
I'll get candles and my mom's lace tablecloth.
我帶蠟燭跟我媽的蕾絲桌布

2
00:00:10,61 --> 00:00:12,70
And since it's Rachel's birthday...
既然是瑞秋的生日…

3
00:00:12,94 --> 00:00:15,14
...I thought I'd poach a salmon.
…我想我煮一條鮭魚

4
00:00:15,98 --> 00:00:16,84
What?
怎麼樣嘛？

5
00:00:17,05 --> 00:00:21,18
Question. Why do we always have parties where you poach things?
我要問為什麼每次開派對 你都要水煮東西啊？

6
00:00:21,38 --> 00:00:22,87
You want to be on the food committee?
你想總掌食物委員會嗎？

7
00:00:23,18 --> 00:00:26,21
Question 2. Why do we always have parties with committees?
問題二，為什麼每次派對 都要有食物委員會？

8
00:00:26,69 --> 00:00:30,52
Why can't we just get pizza and beer and have fun?
為什麼不買些披薩跟啤酒 大家高興就好了嘛？

9
00:00:30,73 --> 00:00:34,79
I agree. Fancy parties are only fun if you're fancy on the inside.
我認為花俏的派對 是給打心底花俏的人的

10
00:00:35,03 --> 00:00:36,69
And I'm not sure we are.
我們又不是這種人

11
00:00:38,17 --> 00:00:40,40
You don't want it to be special?
你們不想要點特別的？

12
00:00:40,70 --> 00:00:43,30
Fine. You can throw any kind of party you want.
很好，你們愛怎麼樣就怎麼樣

13
00:00:43,51 --> 00:00:45,37
Joey,they're not real!
喬伊，那是假的

14
00:00:47,41 --> 00:00:50,57
I start miles beneath the surface of these things. They're fake.
我這裡面空空如也

15
00:00:50,88 --> 00:00:52,37
See? Honk,honk!
看，空空

16
00:00:53,88 --> 00:00:57,05
Wow,it's like porno for clowns!
像給小丑看的小電影

17
00:00:58,69 --> 00:01:00,71
The One With Two Parties
<font color=#38B0DE>-=BT之家DRM小組 http://bbs.btbbt.com=- 河馬壓縮製作 本字幕為河馬根據R3DVD OCR得來</font>

18
00:01:08,92 --> 00:01:15,82
六人行 第2季 第22集 一個頭兩個大

19
00:01:47,10 --> 00:01:49,94
Neither of Rachel's sisters can come.
我跟瑞秋的妹妹講了 她們都不能夠來

20
00:01:50,17 --> 00:01:53,61
I still have to invite Dylan and Emma and Shannon Cooper.
那我還得邀請迪倫 艾瑪，還有古香濃

21
00:01:54,78 --> 00:01:56,00
No Shannon Cooper.
不要香濃

22
00:01:56,21 --> 00:01:57,47
Why not her?
為什麼呢？

23
00:01:57,78 --> 00:01:58,68
Because she....
因為她…

24
00:01:58,88 --> 00:02:00,61
She steals stuff.
會偷東西

25
00:02:03,12 --> 00:02:08,06
Or maybe she doesn't and Joey slept with her and never called her back.
又或許她不會偷東西，但他跟 她上床後就沒再打電話給她了

26
00:02:09,99 --> 00:02:11,62
Joey,that is horrible.
喬伊，那太過份了

27
00:02:11,83 --> 00:02:13,05
Hey,I liked her.
我喜歡她，好嗎？

28
00:02:13,29 --> 00:02:14,63
Maybe too much.
或許太喜歡了

29
00:02:14,86 --> 00:02:16,39
I don't know.
我不知道

30
00:02:16,63 --> 00:02:18,86
I guess I just got scared.
我猜我只是怕了

31
00:02:20,00 --> 00:02:21,83
I'm sorry. I didn't know.
對不起，我不知道

32
00:02:22,84 --> 00:02:25,57
I didn't think anyone would buy that. Okay!
沒想到有人會吃這一套

33
00:02:27,08 --> 00:02:28,51
Hi,honey. How did it go?
蜜糖，好玩嗎？

34
00:02:28,71 --> 00:02:30,64
It was the graduation from hell.
地獄的畢業典禮

35
00:02:30,88 --> 00:02:34,14
My cousin went to hell on a football scholarship.
我表弟是靠足球獎學金 上「地獄大學」的

36
00:02:35,08 --> 00:02:37,38
It's supposed to be a joyous occasion.
這本來應該是個快樂的場合

37
00:02:37,65 --> 00:02:40,71
Nobody thought my sister would graduate from college.
我妹妹從大學畢業了 誰也沒想到

38
00:02:41,19 --> 00:02:45,18
It's a testament to what a girl from Long lsland will do for a Celica.
真正證明了一個長島女孩 為了一部車會做什麼

39
00:02:46,26 --> 00:02:47,16
What happened?
到底怎麼了？

40
00:02:47,36 --> 00:02:48,52
My parents happened.
我寶貝父母呀

41
00:02:48,73 --> 00:02:51,70
All they had to do was sit in the same stadium,smile...
他們只需要坐在同一個體育館 驕傲地微笑…

42
00:02:51,93 --> 00:02:55,10
...and not talk about the divorce. But no!
…絕口不提離婚的事 但不！

43
00:02:55,34 --> 00:02:57,90
They got into a fight during the commencement address.
開幕致詞到一半時 他們就吵得不可開交了

44
00:02:58,17 --> 00:03:02,17
Bishop Tutu actually had to stop and shush them.
主教還得停下來 叫他們兩個住口

45
00:03:04,51 --> 00:03:05,88
You know the good news?
你們知道好消息是什麼嗎？

46
00:03:06,08 --> 00:03:08,74
I get to serve coffee for the next eight hours.
我接著可以幫人 倒八小時的咖啡

47
00:03:10,85 --> 00:03:13,15
I guess we don't invite her parents.
那我們可以不要邀請她父母

48
00:03:13,35 --> 00:03:15,75
-How about just her mom? -Why her mom?
只邀她媽媽，怎麼樣？ 為什麼？

49
00:03:16,22 --> 00:03:18,12
Because I already invited her.
因為我已經邀了

50
00:03:18,73 --> 00:03:20,69
Did you ask Stacy Roth?
你邀了史戴西嗎？

51
00:03:20,93 --> 00:03:22,19
Can't invite her.
不，不能邀她

52
00:03:25,10 --> 00:03:26,43
She also steals.
她也會偷東西

53
00:03:33,27 --> 00:03:36,14
Here are the candles. Where's the birthday cake?
這是生日蛋糕的蠟燭 那生日蛋糕呢？

54
00:03:36,38 --> 00:03:38,28
We're not having birthday cake.
我們不吃生日蛋糕

55
00:03:38,55 --> 00:03:40,28
We're having birthday flan.
我們吃生日派餅

56
00:03:42,62 --> 00:03:43,58
Excuse me?
什麼？

57
00:03:43,79 --> 00:03:45,72
It's a traditional Mexican custard dessert.
是一種傳統墨西哥軟凍點心

58
00:03:45,95 --> 00:03:47,32
That's nice.
不錯呀

59
00:03:47,56 --> 00:03:50,25
Happy birthday,Rachel. Here's some goo!
生日快樂，瑞秋，來些膏

60
00:03:57,07 --> 00:03:58,43
Dr. Greene!
林醫生

61
00:03:58,90 --> 00:04:00,73
Oh,my God! It's Rachel's dad.
老天啊，是瑞秋的爸爸

62
00:04:03,40 --> 00:04:04,67
Why are you here?
你來做什麼？

63
00:04:04,94 --> 00:04:07,64
The father can't see the daughter on her birthday?
怎麼了？女兒生日 老爸過來看看也不行嗎？

64
00:04:07,84 --> 00:04:09,64
No,no,the father can.
不…老爸當然可以

65
00:04:09,91 --> 00:04:13,64
But since I am the roommate, I can tell you she's not here.
但是由於我是她室友 我可以告訴你她不在

66
00:04:13,92 --> 00:04:16,94
And I'll pass along the message. Okay? So bye-bye.
我會轉告她你來過了 所以，拜拜

67
00:04:17,32 --> 00:04:19,08
You're having a party.
你們開派對呀

68
00:04:20,02 --> 00:04:22,01
No,no,not a party.
不，不是派對啦

69
00:04:22,26 --> 00:04:25,35
Just a surprise gathering of some people Rachel knows.
只是一群 瑞秋認識的人的驚喜聚會

70
00:04:25,59 --> 00:04:29,29
-This is Phoebe,Chandler and Joey. -I'll never remember all that.
這是菲比，錢德，喬伊 太多人了我記不住

71
00:04:29,83 --> 00:04:31,86
So what's the deal?
所以你們是要…瑞秋回來

72
00:04:32,13 --> 00:04:35,76
Rachel comes home,people pop out and yell stuff? Is that it?
大家跳出來尖叫 是不是這樣子？

73
00:04:36,00 --> 00:04:39,46
This isn't your first surprise party,is it,sir?
這不是 你的第一個驚喜派對吧？

74
00:04:42,38 --> 00:04:43,87
Hi,Monica.
摩妮卡

75
00:04:46,98 --> 00:04:49,88
The Chinese menu guy. Forgot the menus.
有人送了中餐館菜單來 他忘了菜單了

76
00:04:50,15 --> 00:04:52,81
So basically,just a Chinese guy.
所以基本上只是個中國人而已

77
00:04:54,52 --> 00:04:58,69
Dr. Greene,come with me. We'll put your jacket on Rachel's bed.
林醫生，你跟我來好了 我們把外套放瑞秋床上

78
00:05:01,40 --> 00:05:04,33
All right. That sounds like a two-person job.
好啊，那似乎需要兩個人

79
00:05:07,87 --> 00:05:10,17
Well,my goodness! What was that?
我的天，你剛幹嘛你？

80
00:05:10,41 --> 00:05:14,03
Sandra,I thought you were Rachel. We weren't ready for you yet.
真對不起，我以為你是瑞秋 可是我們還沒準備好

81
00:05:14,24 --> 00:05:18,01
-You thought I was Rachel? -Yes,because you look so young.
你以為我是瑞秋？ 對啊，你看起來好年輕

82
00:05:18,25 --> 00:05:20,81
And because you're both, you know,white women.
而且基本上你們兩個都是… 白種女人

83
00:05:23,55 --> 00:05:27,72
Oh,I missed you kids. Should I put my coat in the bedroom?
我好想念你們 我應該把外套放房間嗎？

84
00:05:30,19 --> 00:05:33,32
-No,I'll take that for you. -Oh,well,thank you.
不，交給我好了 那就謝了

85
00:05:33,56 --> 00:05:35,83
Such a gentleman. Thank you.
真是個紳士啊

86
00:05:38,90 --> 00:05:42,70
It all looks so nice. So festive. All the balloons.
看起來真棒，喜氣洋洋的 那麼多汽球

87
00:05:43,77 --> 00:05:47,26
Oh,the funniest thing happened to me on the way here.
我過來的時候碰見一兩件怪事

88
00:05:47,54 --> 00:05:50,01
-I was driving -That's great!
我在開… 太棒了

89
00:05:53,25 --> 00:05:56,58
I can't wait to hear the rest, but I have to go to the bathroom.
我等不及你說完 我快憋不住了

90
00:05:56,85 --> 00:05:58,51
Hey,come with me.
跟我來

91
00:05:59,02 --> 00:06:01,25
-What? -lt will be like we're gal pals.
什麼？ 就像我們是姐妹

92
00:06:01,52 --> 00:06:04,25
You know,like at a restaurant. It'll be fun! Come on.
你知道，像在餐廳 會很好玩的，來吧…

93
00:06:10,26 --> 00:06:12,06
Oh,my God. Oh,my God. Oh,my God!
天啊…

94
00:06:12,30 --> 00:06:13,79
Think. Think.
想一想，快想一想

95
00:06:14,04 --> 00:06:16,23
What would Jack and Chrissy do?
傑克跟克麗會怎麼做？

96
00:06:18,14 --> 00:06:21,58
Okay,now that your coat is safely in the bed
你的外套安全上床了…

97
00:06:21,81 --> 00:06:24,14
We can come back out in the living room.
我們現在可以回客廳了

98
00:06:24,41 --> 00:06:28,71
Joey and Chandler,it's time you take Dr. Greene over to your place.
對了，喬伊，錢德，我想你們 應該帶林醫生到你們那邊去

99
00:06:28,92 --> 00:06:30,78
Yes,absolutely.
對，完全正確

100
00:06:32,22 --> 00:06:33,05
Why,again?
為什麼？

101
00:06:34,46 --> 00:06:36,92
Because that's where the party is,you goon!
因為派對在那邊呀，呆子

102
00:06:38,66 --> 00:06:42,49
-See,this is just the staging area. -Right,it's the staging area.
這邊只是準備區 對…準備區而已

103
00:06:42,76 --> 00:06:45,73
This is clearly in the wrong apartment.
這個放錯地方了

104
00:06:50,91 --> 00:06:54,47
All right,you guys are off to party number one.
好吧，你們這些去一號派對

105
00:06:55,91 --> 00:06:57,57
And you....
而你們呢…

106
00:06:57,81 --> 00:07:00,25
You are off to party number two.
去二號派對

107
00:07:00,85 --> 00:07:03,98
All right,let's keep it moving, let's keep it moving.
繼續走，繼續走，快

108
00:07:06,29 --> 00:07:08,78
At least send some women to my party.
你至少送些女的來我這邊好嗎

109
00:07:11,03 --> 00:07:12,99
Okay,that's Ross. All right.
是羅斯，好…

110
00:07:14,03 --> 00:07:15,50
Okay,they're coming.
他們來了

111
00:07:22,70 --> 00:07:25,00
Thank you for such a wonderful dinner.
謝謝你美妙的晚餐

112
00:07:25,61 --> 00:07:27,44
Thanks for being born.
謝謝你出生

113
00:07:27,68 --> 00:07:30,74
Thank you for my beautiful earrings. They're perfect.
謝謝你這對漂亮的耳環 真的好美

114
00:07:30,95 --> 00:07:32,11
I love you.
我愛你

115
00:07:32,95 --> 00:07:36,04
Now,you can exchange them if you want,okay?
你要的話可以拿去換

116
00:07:36,78 --> 00:07:38,84
Now I love you even more.
現在我更愛你了

117
00:07:44,36 --> 00:07:45,29
Surprise!
驚喜…

118
00:07:46,13 --> 00:07:47,62
Oh,my gosh!
天啊…

119
00:07:47,86 --> 00:07:48,73
Wow!
哇！

120
00:07:49,96 --> 00:07:51,63
Oh,my God. Mom!
天啊…媽

121
00:07:51,83 --> 00:07:53,13
This is so great!
太棒了

122
00:07:53,53 --> 00:07:55,53
Happy birthday,sweetie.
生日快樂，瑞秋

123
00:07:57,14 --> 00:07:59,77
You! I had no idea!
你…我完全不知

124
00:07:59,97 --> 00:08:01,17
-Really? -No,I knew.
真的？ 不，我知道的

125
00:08:01,41 --> 00:08:02,57
All right.
好

126
00:08:03,68 --> 00:08:05,98
There's food and drinks on the table.
各位，桌上有吃的跟喝的

127
00:08:06,25 --> 00:08:08,84
Go across the hall. Right now,Joey and Chandler's.
現在去對面 喬伊跟錢德那邊，去呀

128
00:08:09,08 --> 00:08:10,35
-Why? -Just go.
為什麼？ 去就是了

129
00:08:13,02 --> 00:08:14,01
Weird.
怪啊

130
00:08:14,22 --> 00:08:15,21
Surprise!
驚喜！

131
00:08:18,86 --> 00:08:20,99
Happy birthday,sweet pea.
生日快樂，小甜豆

132
00:08:21,23 --> 00:08:22,32
Daddy!
爸爸

133
00:08:27,60 --> 00:08:30,57
Both of them are here? Both of them? Both of them are here?
他們都來了，兩個都來了？

134
00:08:30,84 --> 00:08:33,17
Well,we could count again?
我們可以再算一次

135
00:08:33,91 --> 00:08:35,24
I can't believe this!
我無法相信有這種事

136
00:08:35,44 --> 00:08:37,00
You know,this is ridiculous.
這太荒唐了

137
00:08:37,25 --> 00:08:39,51
This is your birthday,your party.
這是你的生日，你的派對

138
00:08:39,71 --> 00:08:42,91
Let's put them together. If they can't deal with it,who cares?
我說把他們放在一起，如果 他們應付不來的話，誰在乎？

139
00:08:43,12 --> 00:08:45,18
-I do. -That's who.
我在乎 就是你

140
00:08:47,09 --> 00:08:48,42
Are you gonna be okay?
你不要緊吧？

141
00:08:48,62 --> 00:08:52,46
I don't really have a choice. I can look at the bright side.
我根本就別無選擇嘛 我可以往好的方面想啊

142
00:08:52,69 --> 00:08:55,56
I get two birthday parties and two birthday cakes.
我有兩個生日派對 還有兩個生日蛋糕

143
00:08:55,80 --> 00:08:57,02
Well,actually...
其實只有…

144
00:08:57,60 --> 00:08:59,73
...just one birthday flan.
…一個生日派餅

145
00:09:02,87 --> 00:09:05,60
It's a traditional Mexican custard dessert.
那是一種墨西哥軟凍點心

146
00:09:05,87 --> 00:09:08,43
Talk to Monica. She's on the food committee.
你去跟摩妮卡講比較好 她是食物委員會的人

147
00:09:15,28 --> 00:09:18,81
Some girl just walked up to me and said,"I want you,Dennis"...
有個女的剛剛走過來跟我說 「我要你，丹尼」…

148
00:09:19,05 --> 00:09:21,45
...and stuck her tongue down my throat.
…然後給了我一個熱吻

149
00:09:21,89 --> 00:09:23,12
I love this party!
我愛這個派對

150
00:09:24,33 --> 00:09:26,42
-Quick volleyball question. -Volleyball.
我有個排球問題 排球？

151
00:09:26,66 --> 00:09:28,63
We set up a court in your room.
我們在你房間弄了個球場

152
00:09:28,83 --> 00:09:31,30
You didn't like that gray lamp,did you?
你不是真的喜歡 那個灰燈，對不對？

153
00:09:32,43 --> 00:09:36,63
A woman stuck her tongue down my throat. I'm not even listening to you.
剛才有個女人給我一個熱吻 我根本就沒聽你說話

154
00:09:37,10 --> 00:09:39,80
-Dennis! -Okay,that's me.
丹尼… 她在叫我了

155
00:09:41,24 --> 00:09:45,18
Can you keep Dad occupied? I'm gonna talk to Mom for a while.
蜜糖，你陪我爸一下，好嗎？ 我要去跟我媽講一下話

156
00:09:45,45 --> 00:09:47,94
Do you have any ideas for any openers?
那我用什麼話當… 當開場白

157
00:09:48,78 --> 00:09:51,84
Stay clear of "I'm the guy that's doing your daughter"...
你只要避開「我是那個上 你女兒的人」…

158
00:09:52,12 --> 00:09:54,11
...and you should be okay.
…就不會有問題了

159
00:09:56,32 --> 00:09:58,32
I want you to take a piece of paper
我要你們一個人拿一張紙…

160
00:09:58,53 --> 00:10:02,49
Here you go. And write down your most embarrassing memory.
拿去 然後寫下你們最臭的回憶

161
00:10:03,00 --> 00:10:07,49
When you're not using the markers, put the caps back on them...
請各位在用完麥克筆之後 把筆蓋蓋上…

162
00:10:07,70 --> 00:10:09,76
... because they will dry out.
…不然的話，筆會幹掉的

163
00:10:10,71 --> 00:10:12,10
Hi,Dr. Greene.
林醫生

164
00:10:13,84 --> 00:10:16,17
So how's everything in the...
血管外科遊戲中…

165
00:10:16,88 --> 00:10:18,85
...vascular surgery...
…的一切…

166
00:10:19,35 --> 00:10:20,18
...game?
…都還好嗎？

167
00:10:21,52 --> 00:10:24,97
It's not a game,Ross. A woman died on my table today.
那不是遊戲，羅斯 今天有個女人死在我手術台上

168
00:10:25,55 --> 00:10:26,82
I'm sorry.
很遺憾

169
00:10:28,86 --> 00:10:31,05
That's the good thing about my job.
那就是我工作的好處

170
00:10:31,29 --> 00:10:34,56
All the dinosaurs on my table are already dead.
因為我在工作台上的那些恐龍 都已經死了

171
00:10:37,20 --> 00:10:39,83
Listen,I don't mean to be a pain about this...
聽著，各位 我並不是故意要煩你們的…

172
00:10:40,03 --> 00:10:43,16
... but I've noticed some of you are just placing them on.
…但我注意到 你們剛剛有些人只是套上

173
00:10:43,37 --> 00:10:45,24
You want to push the caps...
你們應該是要用力按…

174
00:10:47,17 --> 00:10:49,23
... until you hear them click.
…按到喀的一聲為止

175
00:10:51,01 --> 00:10:51,84
Gunther!
阿剛

176
00:10:52,05 --> 00:10:53,01
Where you going?
你要去哪裡啊？

177
00:10:53,21 --> 00:10:55,88
I was sort of thinking about maybe
我…我只是在想，或許我…

178
00:10:56,15 --> 00:10:59,14
No! No,you can't go! No,this is fun.
不…你不能走 不，這很好玩

179
00:10:59,42 --> 00:11:01,89
We're just starting. Here's your marker.
來嘛…我們才剛開始 來，這是你的筆

180
00:11:05,16 --> 00:11:07,89
If you want to go,just go.
聽著，你想走就走好了

181
00:11:08,16 --> 00:11:10,06
She'll yell at me again.
不，她會再吼我

182
00:11:13,43 --> 00:11:15,27
All right,I can get you out.
好吧，我可以把你弄出去

183
00:11:15,50 --> 00:11:16,56
What?
什麼？

184
00:11:18,27 --> 00:11:20,76
In a minute,I'll create a diversion.
等一下我們來個聲東擊西

185
00:11:21,01 --> 00:11:24,67
When I do,walk quickly to the door and don't look back.
到時候，你趕快朝門走 不要回頭

186
00:11:25,71 --> 00:11:28,68
-I think I need a drink. -I'll get it for you.
我想來杯喝的 我去幫你拿

187
00:11:28,92 --> 00:11:30,91
-What do you want? -Scotch.
你要喝什麼？ 威士忌

188
00:11:31,12 --> 00:11:35,45
I'll be back in 10 seconds with your scotch on the rocks in a glass.
好，我十秒鐘之內 會帶著你的威士忌加冰塊回來

189
00:11:35,76 --> 00:11:36,59
Neat!
純

190
00:11:37,26 --> 00:11:38,25
Cool.
正

191
00:11:39,29 --> 00:11:42,13
Neat,as in no rocks.
純的，不加冰塊

192
00:11:43,00 --> 00:11:43,90
I know.
我知道

193
00:11:47,90 --> 00:11:51,30
Hello,Ross! Where have you been?
羅斯，你上哪兒去了？

194
00:11:52,01 --> 00:11:54,87
I have been in the bathroom.
我一直在洗手間

195
00:11:55,91 --> 00:11:58,40
Stay clear of the salmon mousse.
避開那些鮭魚慕斯

196
00:12:02,88 --> 00:12:04,54
Scotch neat.
純威士忌

197
00:12:04,99 --> 00:12:07,08
That's Rachel's father's drink.
瑞秋她爹就愛那玩意兒

198
00:12:09,09 --> 00:12:11,52
Mine too. Isn't that neat?
我也是，很酷，不是嗎？

199
00:12:12,36 --> 00:12:14,05
Scotch neat.
純威士忌

200
00:12:16,73 --> 00:12:18,82
Would you excuse me?
我先失陪了

201
00:12:24,91 --> 00:12:27,57
Where are you sneaking off to,mister?
你想溜到哪裡去呢，先生？

202
00:12:28,58 --> 00:12:30,20
I'm getting my cigarettes.
我要去拿我外套裡的香煙

203
00:12:30,41 --> 00:12:31,34
No.
不…

204
00:12:31,55 --> 00:12:32,91
What do you mean "no"?
什麼意思啊？

205
00:12:33,58 --> 00:12:35,85
See,because that's the staging area.
因為那邊是準備區

206
00:12:36,12 --> 00:12:39,68
You go in there,it'll ruin the whole illusion of the party.
你一去的話 你對派對的幻影就都成空了

207
00:12:40,79 --> 00:12:42,85
Take your scotch back in there...
你還是帶著你的威士忌回去…

208
00:12:43,06 --> 00:12:46,39
...and I will get your cigarettes for you,sir.
…然後我去幫你拿香煙 好嗎？

209
00:12:46,76 --> 00:12:49,86
-Get my glasses too. -All righty-roo.
還有我的眼鏡 有我就搞定了

210
00:12:53,43 --> 00:12:56,56
What a great moment to say that for the first time.
真是第一次說那句話的好時機

211
00:12:59,87 --> 00:13:04,24
Okay,the first person's most embarrassing memory is...
我現在來看看 第一個人的最臭的回憶就是…

212
00:13:04,48 --> 00:13:06,54
... "Monica,your party sucks."
…「摩妮卡，你的派對真遜」

213
00:13:07,65 --> 00:13:08,95
Very funny.
非常幽默

214
00:13:09,62 --> 00:13:12,92
Oh,no! Did someone forget to use a coaster?
天啊，有人忘了用杯墊嗎？

215
00:13:13,12 --> 00:13:14,28
What?
什麼？

216
00:13:21,46 --> 00:13:22,93
I don't see anything.
我沒有看到呀

217
00:13:23,76 --> 00:13:26,39
Great,I'm seeing water rings again.
是嗎？我的眼睛又花了

218
00:13:29,40 --> 00:13:31,80
Ross,whose glasses are those?
羅斯，那是誰的眼鏡啊？

219
00:13:32,74 --> 00:13:33,80
Mine.
我的

220
00:13:35,58 --> 00:13:37,10
You wear bifocals?
你戴遠近兩用的眼鏡？

221
00:13:39,18 --> 00:13:42,24
I have a condition apparently...
我的視力…

222
00:13:42,45 --> 00:13:44,31
...that I require...
…顯然同時…

223
00:13:45,79 --> 00:13:48,08
...two different sets of focals.
…需要用到兩種鏡片

224
00:13:49,12 --> 00:13:52,52
Do you know my husband has glasses just like that?
你知道我先生也有一副 跟你一樣的眼鏡嗎？

225
00:13:52,76 --> 00:13:55,42
Well,those are very popular frames.
那副鏡框很流行

226
00:13:55,70 --> 00:13:57,79
Neil Sedaka wears them.
尼爾席達卡也有一副

227
00:14:00,77 --> 00:14:03,26
I hear you can get people out of here.
聽說你有辦法弄我們出去 是不是？

228
00:14:07,34 --> 00:14:10,54
You didn't tell me your boyfriend smokes.
你並沒有告訴我你男友會抽煙

229
00:14:10,78 --> 00:14:12,18
Yeah,like a chimney.
對，像根煙囪

230
00:14:13,95 --> 00:14:15,11
Big smoker.
大煙槍

231
00:14:16,72 --> 00:14:18,48
Big,big smoker.
超大煙槍

232
00:14:18,79 --> 00:14:22,69
In fact,I'm gonna go into the hallway and fire up this bad boy.
事實上，我現在就去走廊上 點燃這根大壞蛋了

233
00:14:36,54 --> 00:14:38,06
Are you wearing my glasses?
你在戴我的眼鏡嗎？

234
00:14:39,57 --> 00:14:40,54
Yes.
對

235
00:14:43,21 --> 00:14:47,08
I was just warming up the earpieces for you.
我只是在替你 把那個耳架弄暖一點

236
00:14:48,02 --> 00:14:48,98
Thank you.
謝謝

237
00:14:51,59 --> 00:14:53,55
Is that one of my cigarettes?
那是我的香煙嗎？

238
00:15:00,09 --> 00:15:04,00
Yes,it is. I was just moistening the tip.
對，沒錯 我在把這個煙屁股弄濕

239
00:15:05,93 --> 00:15:09,33
She's taking the trash out, so I can get you out of here.
好了，她去倒垃圾了 我可以弄你們出去了

240
00:15:09,60 --> 00:15:11,94
But it has to be now. She'll be back any minute.
可是你們得馬上走 她隨時會回來

241
00:15:12,21 --> 00:15:13,10
What about my friend?
那我朋友呢？

242
00:15:13,34 --> 00:15:16,87
Only the three of you. Any more and she'll get suspicious.
不行，只有你們三個 超過三個她就會起疑心的

243
00:15:17,08 --> 00:15:19,67
-Let me just get my coat. -There isn't time!
好吧，我去拿外套 沒有時間了

244
00:15:22,12 --> 00:15:23,58
Just leave everything.
什麼都不要拿

245
00:15:24,05 --> 00:15:26,35
They'll take care of you next door.
隔壁那些人會照顧你們的

246
00:15:26,92 --> 00:15:28,75
Is it true they have beer?
他們有啤酒是真的嗎？

247
00:15:30,02 --> 00:15:32,36
Everything you've heard is true.
你聽到的都是真的

248
00:15:33,23 --> 00:15:35,59
Could you guys please keep it down?
你們小聲一點，好不好？

249
00:15:35,80 --> 00:15:38,59
We're trying to start a Boggle tournament.
我們要來個文字遊戲錦標賽

250
00:15:43,74 --> 00:15:44,57
You!
你

251
00:15:44,81 --> 00:15:45,90
And you.
還有你

252
00:15:46,14 --> 00:15:48,04
You're supposed to be at my party.
你們應該在我的派對的啊

253
00:15:48,31 --> 00:15:50,14
And Gunther!
還有阿剛

254
00:15:54,75 --> 00:15:56,38
What are you doing here?
你在這個地方幹什麼啊？

255
00:16:00,29 --> 00:16:01,98
Welcome to the fo
歡迎光臨…

256
00:16:06,13 --> 00:16:09,06
All right,I'm sorry. But these people needed me.
好吧，對不起嘛 可是這些人需要我啊

257
00:16:09,26 --> 00:16:11,56
They work hard all week. It's Saturday night.
他們辛苦了一個禮拜 今天是週末

258
00:16:11,77 --> 00:16:14,00
They deserve to have a little fun. Go!
他們有權享一點兒樂的，去

259
00:16:15,24 --> 00:16:17,00
You know,my party is fun.
我的派對很好玩

260
00:16:17,27 --> 00:16:19,90
It's a little quieter, less obvious sort of fun.
或許是安靜了一點吧 比較含蓄的樂趣

261
00:16:20,11 --> 00:16:23,24
But if people would just give it a chance,it's
但如果大家給它一個機會 那會比較…

262
00:16:27,51 --> 00:16:32,08
-You want me to see a therapist? -Sweetheart,you have a problem.
你要我去看心理醫生？ 親愛的，你顯然有問題了

263
00:16:32,29 --> 00:16:35,95
You've chosen a boyfriend exactly like your father.
你居然選了一個 跟你爸一模一樣的男朋友

264
00:16:36,82 --> 00:16:39,16
Okay,Mom,I'll make an appointment.
媽，我會先去掛號的

265
00:16:39,43 --> 00:16:42,62
But right now,I gotta go. I gotta go do a thing.
現在我得走了 我得去做一件事

266
00:16:42,83 --> 00:16:47,70
Did you know your mother spent $1200 on bonsai trees?
你知道嗎？你老媽居然花了 一千二百塊買一個盆栽

267
00:16:48,10 --> 00:16:49,83
I felt like Gulliver.
我覺得我好像巨人在小森林裡

268
00:16:50,87 --> 00:16:53,70
Daddy,I really want to hear more about this...
爸，你知道嗎？ 我真的很想再多聽，真的…

269
00:16:53,97 --> 00:16:57,14
...but I just have to do some stuff.
…但我有點事要處理

270
00:16:57,34 --> 00:17:00,34
You work and you work and you work at a marriage...
我一直很努力 想要挽救我們的婚姻…

271
00:17:00,55 --> 00:17:02,95
... but all he cares about is his stupid boat.
…可是他只關心他那艘蠢船

272
00:17:03,22 --> 00:17:05,98
You work and you work and you work on a boat.
我一直一直努力的去弄我的船

273
00:17:06,22 --> 00:17:09,12
He always ridiculed my pottery classes.
他老是嘲笑我的燒陶課

274
00:17:09,36 --> 00:17:11,29
And you sand it and varnish it.
磨好了之後還要上釉

275
00:17:11,53 --> 00:17:15,15
But when all is said and done, he still drinks out of the mugs.
但他還是用我做的杯子喝東西

276
00:17:15,36 --> 00:17:18,35
One night of her yoga and Bridges of Madison County....
聽她念一晚她的瑜珈 還有她的「麥迪遜之橋」…

277
00:17:18,63 --> 00:17:21,40
-The scotch,the cigarettes.... - The bonsais and the Chihuahua....
威士忌，香煙… 盆栽和吉娃娃狗…

278
00:17:21,64 --> 00:17:23,90
I may have only been in therapy for three weeks now but
我或許只看了 三個禮拜的心理醫生，但…

279
00:17:24,17 --> 00:17:26,64
What the hell does she want with half a boat?
她要半條船幹什麼？

280
00:17:30,51 --> 00:17:34,04
Okay,okay,you can be shirts and I'll be skins.
你衣服留著我光著身子好了

281
00:17:35,02 --> 00:17:36,85
I'll be skins!
我光身子呀

282
00:17:43,59 --> 00:17:45,85
How you holding up there,tiger?
你沒事吧，老虎？

283
00:17:47,56 --> 00:17:51,43
Sorry. When my parents were getting divorced,I got a lot of "tigers."
很抱歉，我父母在鬧離婚時 很多人叫我「老虎」

284
00:17:52,27 --> 00:17:55,70
I got a lot of "champs," "chiefs," "sports."
很多人叫我 「冠軍」「老大」「君子」

285
00:17:56,04 --> 00:17:57,23
I even got a "governor."
還有人叫我「州長」

286
00:17:59,77 --> 00:18:03,17
This is it,isn't it? This is what my life will be like.
就這樣了，是不是？ 我的生活就會變成這樣

287
00:18:03,54 --> 00:18:05,60
My mom there,my dad there.
我媽跟我爸一人一個地方

288
00:18:05,91 --> 00:18:08,40
Thanksgiving,Christmas.
感恩節，聖誕節

289
00:18:08,62 --> 00:18:13,21
She gets the house,he's in a condo my sister will decorate with wicker.
她得到房子，他住在我妹用 柳條傢俱幫他佈置的公寓

290
00:18:14,02 --> 00:18:16,25
How did you get through this?
錢德，你是怎麼熬過來的？

291
00:18:18,43 --> 00:18:21,36
I relied on a carefully regimented program...
我利用了我精心策劃的計劃…

292
00:18:21,60 --> 00:18:23,12
...of denial...
…拒絕面對現實…

293
00:18:24,06 --> 00:18:25,93
...and wetting the bed.
…還有尿床

294
00:18:28,77 --> 00:18:31,10
You know,I just It's so weird.
這太詭異了

295
00:18:31,37 --> 00:18:36,04
I mean,I was in there just listening to them bitch about each other.
我是說，我人在裡面 卻聽著他們兩個人罵來罵去

296
00:18:36,24 --> 00:18:39,04
All I kept thinking about was the Fourth of July.
可是心裡卻一直在想著國慶日

297
00:18:40,65 --> 00:18:42,58
Because it reminded you of the way...
因為那讓你想起我們的祖先…

298
00:18:42,78 --> 00:18:45,48
...our forefathers used to bitch at each other?
…從前也是罵來罵去的嗎？

299
00:18:46,39 --> 00:18:49,05
It's just this thing. Every year we would...
是這樣子的啦 我們每年…

300
00:18:49,29 --> 00:18:52,05
...go out on my dad's boat and watch the fireworks.
…都會坐我爸的船出海 去看煙火

301
00:18:52,59 --> 00:18:56,62
Mom always hated it because the ocean air made her hair all big.
可是我媽討厭去 因為海風會把她的頭髮吹膨

302
00:18:56,83 --> 00:18:59,99
My sister Jill would be throwing up over the side...
我妹妹吉兒 則會靠在船邊嘔吐…

303
00:19:00,33 --> 00:19:03,00
...and Dad would be upset because nobody helped.
…我爸會不高興 因為沒有人幫他忙

304
00:19:03,27 --> 00:19:06,40
And when we did help,he'd scream at us for doing it wrong.
當我們幫忙的時候呢 他又會吼叫說我們越幫越忙

305
00:19:09,61 --> 00:19:13,81
But then when the fireworks started, everybody just shut up.
但是當煙火開始的時候 大家都閉嘴了

306
00:19:14,35 --> 00:19:16,61
You know,and it'd get really cold.
然後天氣會變得很冷

307
00:19:16,85 --> 00:19:20,48
And we'd all just sort of smoosh under this one blanket.
我們會全部都擠在 一條毯子下面

308
00:19:20,75 --> 00:19:23,85
It never occurred to anybody to bring another one.
從來沒有人想到要多帶一條來

309
00:19:25,59 --> 00:19:27,03
And now it's....
但是現在…

310
00:19:30,76 --> 00:19:32,16
Yeah,I know.
對，我知道

311
00:19:55,49 --> 00:19:57,48
Thanks for coming. I hope you had fun.
謝謝光臨，希望你們玩得開心

312
00:19:57,89 --> 00:19:59,88
All right,I'm hitting the road.
好了，我要走了

313
00:20:00,13 --> 00:20:03,03
Now,I've left my 10 verbs on the table.
我把十個動詞放在你桌上了

314
00:20:03,23 --> 00:20:05,53
Be sure and send me that finished poem.
一定要把完成的詩寄給我

315
00:20:05,80 --> 00:20:07,66
Okay,will do. Glad you came.
我會的，很高興你來了

316
00:20:07,97 --> 00:20:11,03
-I think I saw Rachel out in the hall. -Let me go check.
我想我看到瑞秋在走廊上 我去看看

317
00:20:13,74 --> 00:20:15,67
Your mom wants to say goodbye.
你媽要跟你道別了

318
00:20:15,98 --> 00:20:17,91
Happy birthday,sweetie.
生日快樂，親愛的

319
00:20:21,15 --> 00:20:22,17
You drive safe.
小心開車

320
00:20:23,98 --> 00:20:25,35
What are you doing?
羅斯，你在幹嘛？

321
00:20:26,72 --> 00:20:30,09
I'm getting ready for the water skiing.
我正在為去滑水做準備

322
00:20:30,32 --> 00:20:32,59
Okay,big hug. One more. Come on!
來呀，抱抱

323
00:20:35,60 --> 00:20:36,72
How are you?
你好嗎？

324
00:20:39,17 --> 00:20:41,10
-Where are you going? -To get my coat.
林醫生，你要去哪裡？ 拿我的外套

325
00:20:41,37 --> 00:20:42,77
We'll get that for you.
我們去拿

326
00:20:43,04 --> 00:20:46,01
All right,all right. I can get my own coat.
好了…我可以自己去，好嗎？

327
00:20:53,78 --> 00:20:56,37
Sorry,we're on a major flan high.
抱歉，派餅讓我們爽歪了

328
00:20:59,09 --> 00:21:01,85
Oh,no. No,you're not supposed to be here.
不對…你不應該來這裡的

329
00:21:02,09 --> 00:21:05,42
This is the staging area. It's all wrong. You should leave.
因為這裡是準備區 全弄錯了，你應該走

330
00:21:06,13 --> 00:21:08,46
You know,just get out.
出去就是了

331
00:21:17,37 --> 00:21:19,64
Or perhaps you'd like a creme de menthe.
要不要來杯薄荷酒啊？

332
00:21:21,21 --> 00:21:23,30
I have to be heading toward my chateau.
我必須打道回府了，謝了

333
00:21:23,58 --> 00:21:26,38
I guess we're going back into the hallway again.
好吧，那麼我猜 我們又要回到走廊了

334
00:21:26,61 --> 00:21:28,58
Thanks for coming,Mrs. Greene.
謝謝光臨，林太太

335
00:21:41,40 --> 00:21:42,89
You take care.
保重了

336
00:21:46,43 --> 00:21:48,06
Oh,you kids.
你們這些孩子

337
00:21:50,94 --> 00:21:51,80
Well.
這麼嘛…

338
00:21:53,51 --> 00:21:56,64
This is the best party I've been to in years.
好久沒有參加這麼棒的派對了

339
00:21:57,61 --> 00:21:58,77
Thank you!
謝謝

340
00:22:04,62 --> 00:22:06,78
Okay,everybody, it's time for flan!
各位，切派餅了

341
00:22:07,02 --> 00:22:10,35
Yep! Get ready for the gelatinous fun.
對，準備享用凍凍樂了

342
00:22:11,36 --> 00:22:14,73
Looks like that stuff you get when you get an infection.
看起來有點像 傷口發炎時化的膿

343
00:22:14,96 --> 00:22:16,72
Okay,that's enough.
好了，夠了

344
00:22:16,96 --> 00:22:19,73
Okay,Rachel, make a special flan wish.
瑞秋，許個派餅願吧

345
00:22:21,03 --> 00:22:22,63
Okay,I've got one.
好了

346
00:22:26,94 --> 00:22:28,07
Heads up!
小心！

347
00:22:30,08 --> 00:22:33,14
Wow! Those things almost never come true.
這很少有實現的時候的

348
00:00:00,00 --> 00:00:00,00


349
00:00:00,00 --> 00:00:00,00


